# a-crew-member-comes-home — plan 15 C2, and plan 14 H4 closed.
#
# The arc `DESIGN.md` § 9 describes, played end to end in one run: a
# crew member blocks a corridor, is destroyed, and lies there — until
# somebody drives out, picks the wreck up, carries it to the core and
# waits out the recovery clock.
#
# ⚠ **`roster` falls to 0 and comes back to 1, and that pair is the
# file.**  `helper <i> <q> <r>` cannot tell the story: a wreck keeps its
# roster slot and its hex (plan 14 H3), so "helper 0 is at (6, 0)" is
# true whether it is standing there or lying there.
#
# ⚠ **Nothing here presses a key to clear or to earn**, and only two
# lines press one at all.  `DESIGN.md` § 11 gives ONE context-resolved
# key — empty hands = pickup, carrying = deposit — and `take` / `drop`
# are its two outcomes written out, because a script says what it means.
#
# ⚠ **The corridor is one hex wide on purpose.**  A vehicle is only a
# blocker where the wave has nowhere to go round (plan 13 V5), so this
# is the map that can lose a crew member at all — and it is also why
# fetching one costs something: the hex the wreck is on is the hex the
# wave is coming through.

echo a crew member comes home: lost in the corridor, carried back, on the roster again

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 11 0
marker 11 0 spawn 3

count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

# One row, and nothing beside it.
palette 5
drag -3 0 14 0
count painted 18 18

# The player waits at the core; the crew member stands in the corridor.
park 0 0
vehicle 0 0
crew 6 0
helper 0 6 0
roster 1 1
cargo 0 0

wave 1
count alive 1 1

# ── It blocks, and it is destroyed ──────────────────────────────
#
# 50 HP at the blocker rate of 5 HP/s is ten seconds, and the walk out
# is four hexes.
tick 28
roster 0 0
cargo 1 1

# ── The player drives out to fetch it ───────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ Straight through the wave, which is not a mistake: an enemy is not
# something the player bumps into (`DESIGN.md` § 8), so the drive out is
# free and standing still in the corridor is what costs.
drive 6 0
tick 3
vehicle 6 0

take player
cargo 1 1

# ── And carries it home ─────────────────────────────────────────
drive 0 0
tick 3
vehicle 0 0

drop player
cargo 0 0
roster 0 0

# ── Sixty seconds of recovery ───────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ **Exactly 90 ticks, and the last one matters.**  60.0 s over a
# 1/1.5 s tick divides exactly, which is the only case where the
# banked-timer epsilon bites — without it this reads 91 and the line
# below is red by one tick.  See `tests/15_c2_recovery.loft`.
tick 89
roster 0 0

tick 1
roster 1 1
helper 0 0 0

snap c2_a_crew_member_comes_home
